// expect-error: double free:
// BUG-959 note: the reason is unchanged — this IS a double free and is still
// rejected as one — but the WORDING lost the word "deferred". The old message came
// from zercheck's AST scan of defer bodies, which knew the free came from a defer.
// The body is now ordinary IR walked by the CFG, which reports it as any other
// double free. The directive asserts the reason the rule is supposed to give, not
// the phrasing, so it is relaxed to `double free:` rather than pinned to text the
// mechanism no longer produces. The lost specificity is recorded in
// docs/limitations.md as a known cost with a fix sketch.
// The other half of BUG-812. Once a deferred extern destructor is recognised as
// a free, `dev_close(dev); defer dev_close(dev);` is a genuine double free —
// the deferred one fires at scope exit on an already-closed handle. Before
// BUG-812 the deferred call was not a free at all, so nothing was reported.
*opaque dev_open();
void dev_close(*opaque d);

u32 main() {
    *opaque dev = dev_open();
    defer dev_close(dev);
    dev_close(dev);
    return 0;
}
